/*
 * Fuzz target labels, and the build conditions that decide which of
 * them exist in this binary.
 *
 * GENERATED by fuzzing/ledger/targets.py from the call sites of
 * apply_mutation() and friends, plus the Makefile blocks that decide
 * which objects are linked. Do not edit: regenerate with
 *
 *     python3 fuzzing/ledger/targets.py . --emit-c \
 *             > src/common/fuzz_targets.h
 *
 * and check it has not gone stale with --check.
 *
 * Why the guards are here rather than a flat list: the inventory is
 * announced once per run and the ledger subtracts what it saw from it
 * to report what was never reached. A flat list makes every binary
 * announce every label, so hostapd reports the station's targets as
 * NEVER REACHED and the station reports hostapd's. A target that is
 * not in this process is not a target that was missed, and a report
 * that cannot tell them apart buries the second in the first.
 */

